WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
When it's time to celebrate, we do it together.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.333
Yeah,

3
00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:05.526
and when it's time to eat, we stay close to our plates.

4
00:00:05.526 --> 00:00:06.530
(laughing)

5
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.900
And I don't do anything without

6
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.200
the best date in town, Ross Matthews.

7
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.550
(audience cheering)

8
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.840
But you can't have an Emmy party without something to eat.

9
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.650
I mean, right?

10
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.490
All right, so here to present some spectacular snacks

11
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.070
and sips is a woman I love so much.

12
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.117
I actually wrote a cookbook with her.

13
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:30.790
That's right.

14
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.623
It comes out in November.

15
00:00:31.623 --> 00:00:33.580
It's called "Rebel Homemaker,"

16
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.540
and I think we are rebel homemakers.

17
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.484
It's Chef Pilar Valdes.

18
00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:40.800
(audience cheering)

19
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.633
Now, Pilar,

20
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:45.180
you have a real knack for pairing food

21
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.530
with the nominees and coming up with a pithy pun.

22
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.190
So, I'm going to let you take it away.

23
00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.515
What's our first one?

24
00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:52.348
All right.

25
00:00:52.348 --> 00:00:55.490
So, today we have four bites inspired by the nominees.

26
00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:59.447 line:15%
First step, we have Kate Winslettuce cups.

27
00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:01.050 line:15%
(audience laughing)

28
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.680 line:15%
So here, we have this wonderful bite.

29
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.240 line:15%
It's inspired by a Thai pork dish,

30
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.460 line:15%
but you could actually use a ground chicken

31
00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.293 line:15%
or ground turkey,

32
00:01:10.293 --> 00:01:11.470 line:15%
or if you want to keep it vegetarian,

33
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.490 line:15%
you could also do mushroom or cauliflower.

34
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.660 line:15%
You get the crunch from the lettuce,

35
00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.940
a lot of savoriness from the pork,

36
00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.410
and then a ton of herbs and a little bit of chili.

37
00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.667
The flavor in that one bite.

38
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.740
(audience cheers)

39
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.653
All that herb, the chili.

40
00:01:29.523 --> 00:01:30.590
And is it healthy?

41
00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.800
It is, it actually really is.

42
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.123
God, I love this!

43
00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:35.730
(laughter)

44
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.257
We want it to be that show that wasn't like--

45
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.265
Literally--

46
00:01:42.265 --> 00:01:44.043
(laughter)

47
00:01:44.043 --> 00:01:44.876
(audience cheering)

48
00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:46.540
You know it's good when everybody gets quiet.

49
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.106
Yes, exactly.

50
00:01:48.106 --> 00:01:49.270
That makes the cook happy.

51
00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.610
I am very, very happy.

52
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.650
Shall we move on?

53
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.483
Yes.

54
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:56.240
Okay, so next up, in honor of one of the nominees,

55
00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.240 line:15%
the dish is Jason Sudeggkis.

56
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.570 line:15%
(laughing)

57
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.160 line:15%
It's a deviled egg,

58
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.120 line:15%
very classic,

59
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.000 line:15%
but with a little bit of a spin.

60
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.780 line:15%
I like to put a little bit of hot sauce

61
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.066 line:15%
and a little bit of pickled brine in my deviled eggs.

62
00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:12.540 line:15%
Ooh, smart!

63
00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.910 line:15%
Mm-hmm. Shall we?

64
00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.610 line:15%
This is Egg Lasso.

65
00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.613
There you go!

66
00:02:18.806 --> 00:02:21.056
(laughing)

67
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.570
I like to do a little topping bar.

68
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.240 line:15%
So if you have people over,

69
00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.770 line:15%
you can do a little bacon bits,

70
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.700 line:15%
you can do a little toasted breadcrumbs,

71
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.880 line:15%
you could do more pickles,

72
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.440
and then have it be like

73
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.800
a choose your own adventure kind of thing.

74
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.633
I love that.

75
00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:34.466
You guys hear that?

76
00:02:34.466 --> 00:02:35.920
A topping bar for deviled eggs.

77
00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.630
I've never been happier, Pilar.

78
00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.398
That is the most brilliant--

79
00:02:39.398 --> 00:02:40.231
(Pilar laughs)

80
00:02:40.231 --> 00:02:41.733
I have one thing to say to that.

81
00:02:43.445 --> 00:02:45.774
(laughing)

82
00:02:45.774 --> 00:02:47.000
You're going to hate the next one. Go on.

83
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.297
They can definitely mix. I'm like,

84
00:02:48.297 --> 00:02:49.782
"Ooh, it's so good."

85
00:02:49.782 --> 00:02:50.615
Oh my God.

86
00:02:50.615 --> 00:02:51.678
(laughing)

87
00:02:51.678 --> 00:02:52.620
Oh my God.

88
00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.320
All right. So, how are we doing guys?

89
00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.153
I'm not even listening.

90
00:02:57.153 --> 00:02:58.836
I'm just eating. Sorry.

91
00:02:58.836 --> 00:02:59.669
(laughing)

92
00:02:59.669 --> 00:03:00.865
I'm going to,

93
00:03:00.865 --> 00:03:02.530
I'm going to roll in and move on to the next.

94
00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.520 line:15%
The next thing we have is Issa Crudi-rae.

95
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.080 line:15%
I love this.

96
00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.340 line:15%
Issa-- Wait, say it again.

97
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.460 line:15%
Issa Crudi-rae.

98
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.725 line:15%
Okay, I see what you did.

99
00:03:11.725 --> 00:03:14.955 line:15%
Coup d'etat, crudi-rae. Okay.

100
00:03:14.955 --> 00:03:16.030 line:15%
That's so good.

101
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.437 line:15%
You were selling that when you were a little insecure.

102
00:03:18.437 --> 00:03:20.573 line:15%
(laughing)

103
00:03:20.573 --> 00:03:22.108 line:15%
You!

104
00:03:22.108 --> 00:03:23.171 line:15%
You!

105
00:03:23.171 --> 00:03:24.709
(chuckling)

106
00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:25.542
I'm like stupid.

107
00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:26.820
Where do I go from that?

108
00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.710
(laughing)

109
00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:30.910
So this one, Drew,

110
00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.080
takes another of your loves of French onion soup.

111
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.003
We made it into a French onion dip.

112
00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.240
Caramelized onions,

113
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.620
Worcestershire sauce,

114
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.070
hot paprika,

115
00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.090
and then it's in a creamy base.

116
00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.000
It's really good.

117
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:44.833
We lightened it up.

118
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:47.520
We actually use Greek yogurt instead of like,

119
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.820
the heavier stuff.

120
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.653
You guys.

121
00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:52.218
This is so good.

122
00:03:52.218 --> 00:03:53.051
I mean, look how good that is.

123
00:03:53.051 --> 00:03:55.570
And I love that they're also served in little cups.

124
00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.670
You can also put it on a platter if you'd like,

125
00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.530
but put it in a cup.

126
00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.239 line:15%
This is all me.

127
00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:03.051 line:15%
(laughing)

128
00:04:03.051 --> 00:04:04.170 line:15%
Listen, you could put potato chips with this.

129
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.750 line:15%
Oh yeah.

130
00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.040
And I will.

131
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.018
Yeah. Uh-huh.

132
00:04:08.018 --> 00:04:09.040
Yes, a hundred percent. Okay.

133
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.970
Last up.

134
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.803
You guys ready?

135
00:04:10.803 --> 00:04:11.930
Yes.

136
00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.300
In honor of the TV show, "This Is Us,"

137
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.919 line:15%
we have "This is Truffs."

138
00:04:17.919 --> 00:04:20.700 line:15%
(audience laughing)

139
00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.530 line:15%
We have some beautiful, decadent, chocolate truffles.

140
00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.180 line:15%
Everyone thinks, "Oh my God, truffles. They're so fancy."

141
00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.160 line:15%
No, they're really dead simple to make.

142
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.180 line:15%
You just have a ganache,

143
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.710 line:15%
which has equal parts melted chocolate and cream,

144
00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.660
scoop it out with an ice cream scoop

145
00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.320
and then you roll it in additional melted chocolate.

146
00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.430
So it has like--

147
00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.205
I understand why you love Pilar, now.

148
00:04:42.205 --> 00:04:43.060
(Pilar laughs)

149
00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:43.893
When you were just saying, like,

150
00:04:43.893 --> 00:04:44.726
"I really love her,"

151
00:04:44.726 --> 00:04:45.730
I was like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah."

152
00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.583
No, I get it.

153
00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:48.930
I think I really love her right now.

154
00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.271
I just had a whole moment.

155
00:04:50.271 --> 00:04:51.850
Oh, I'm so glad.

156
00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.215
I had a complete moment over here.

157
00:04:54.215 --> 00:04:56.770
(laughing)

158
00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.190
I mean, chocolate and chocolate.

159
00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.530
With the little salt.

160
00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:04.200 line:15%
Yes. So again, like taking the same idea from the,

161
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.810 line:15%
the deviled egg bar, you can roll it in multiple things.

162
00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.960
You could do it with sea salt

163
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.690
or just have a side of pomegranate.

164
00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:13.523
Hello, lover.

165
00:05:13.523 --> 00:05:14.540
Ooh, pomegranate!

166
00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.880
Yeah.

167
00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.563
Ross, I'm going to need you to take us into break.

168
00:05:18.563 --> 00:05:20.070
(laughing)

169
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.440
I got your back.

170
00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.963
Let's hear it for Chef Pilar!

171
00:05:23.963 --> 00:05:26.403
(audience cheers)

172
00:05:26.403 --> 00:05:27.768
Thank you so much.

173
00:05:27.768 --> 00:05:29.795 line:15%
And head over to TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com

174
00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:30.628 line:15%
for the full recipes.

175
00:05:30.628 --> 00:05:32.313 line:15%
You're going to want to make this during the show.

